{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-64276" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+y=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/state.json" "file_sha256" "db29583229ee19e7ec41ee5464bc69bf5bded44515119337e03a03b2fd10bc34"} {"question" "q-64276" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+1 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =\\pm \\text{i}$, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe particular solution of the inhomogeneous equation cannot be of the form $\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ because this is already included in the complementary function. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\ny_p = x (\\alpha \\cos x + \\beta \\sin x),\n]\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & =(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\ {y}_{p}^{″} & =2(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n2(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n-2\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\ -2\\alpha =8\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-4$ and $\\beta =0.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny={y}_{c}+{y}_{p}=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/state.json" "file_sha256" "db29583229ee19e7ec41ee5464bc69bf5bded44515119337e03a03b2fd10bc34"} {"question" "q-64276" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "04f0f5b03a1eed193771446f42328616d0f5d26cce05874a2cf5e6f422fce0ed"} {"question" "q-64276" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/state.json" "file_sha256" "db29583229ee19e7ec41ee5464bc69bf5bded44515119337e03a03b2fd10bc34"} {"question" "q-64276" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["math" "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["math" "y=P{e}^{x}+Qx{e}^{x}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["math" "y=P{e}^{x}+Q{e}^{-x}+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/state.json" "file_sha256" "db29583229ee19e7ec41ee5464bc69bf5bded44515119337e03a03b2fd10bc34"} {"question" "q-64276" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/state.json" "file_sha256" "db29583229ee19e7ec41ee5464bc69bf5bded44515119337e03a03b2fd10bc34"} {"question" "q-79633" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}-2y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/state.json" "file_sha256" "db29583229ee19e7ec41ee5464bc69bf5bded44515119337e03a03b2fd10bc34"} {"question" "q-79633" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}-2y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -2 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =-1$ or $\\lambda =2$, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{2x}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {y}^{″} & =-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-2(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives:\n\n$$\n(-3\\alpha -\\beta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+(\\alpha -3\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-3\\alpha -\\beta =3\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\ \\alpha -3\\beta =-1\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-1,$ $\\beta =0.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{2x}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nNow let us find constants $A$ and $B.$ \n\nSubstituting $y(0)=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA+B-1=0.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-1.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-A{e}^{-x}+2B{e}^{2x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=-1$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n-A+2B=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following system of equations for $A$ and $B$:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}A+B=1 \\\\ -A+2B=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=1,$ $B=0.$\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-x}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/state.json" "file_sha256" "db29583229ee19e7ec41ee5464bc69bf5bded44515119337e03a03b2fd10bc34"} {"question" "q-79633" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "04f0f5b03a1eed193771446f42328616d0f5d26cce05874a2cf5e6f422fce0ed"} {"question" "q-79633" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/state.json" "file_sha256" "db29583229ee19e7ec41ee5464bc69bf5bded44515119337e03a03b2fd10bc34"} {"question" "q-79633" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-2{e}^{2x}+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "y=2{e}^{2x}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "y={e}^{-x}+2{e}^{2x}-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x."] ["math" "y={e}^{-x}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "y={e}^{2x}-{e}^{-x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/state.json" "file_sha256" "db29583229ee19e7ec41ee5464bc69bf5bded44515119337e03a03b2fd10bc34"} {"question" "q-79633" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y={e}^{-x}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/state.json" "file_sha256" "db29583229ee19e7ec41ee5464bc69bf5bded44515119337e03a03b2fd10bc34"} {"question" "q-93819" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-4y=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nhas the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{2x},$ find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/state.json" "file_sha256" "db29583229ee19e7ec41ee5464bc69bf5bded44515119337e03a03b2fd10bc34"} {"question" "q-93819" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.$ So we assume the particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x} & =-2\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+2\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =-4\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-4\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(-4\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-4\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)-4(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n-8\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-8\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-8\\alpha =8\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x) \\\\ -8\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-1,$ $\\beta =0.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/state.json" "file_sha256" "db29583229ee19e7ec41ee5464bc69bf5bded44515119337e03a03b2fd10bc34"} {"question" "q-93819" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "04f0f5b03a1eed193771446f42328616d0f5d26cce05874a2cf5e6f422fce0ed"} {"question" "q-93819" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/state.json" "file_sha256" "db29583229ee19e7ec41ee5464bc69bf5bded44515119337e03a03b2fd10bc34"} {"question" "q-93819" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}_{p}=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x"] ["math" "{y}_{p}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x"] ["math" "{y}_{p}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x"] ["math" "{y}_{p}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x"] ["math" "{y}_{p}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/state.json" "file_sha256" "db29583229ee19e7ec41ee5464bc69bf5bded44515119337e03a03b2fd10bc34"} {"question" "q-93819" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}_{p}=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/state.json" "file_sha256" "db29583229ee19e7ec41ee5464bc69bf5bded44515119337e03a03b2fd10bc34"} {"question" "q-93824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+36y=-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x\n$$\n\nhas the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x,$ find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/state.json" "file_sha256" "db29583229ee19e7ec41ee5464bc69bf5bded44515119337e03a03b2fd10bc34"} {"question" "q-93824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The particular solution of the inhomogeneous equation cannot be of the form $\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡6x$ because this is already included in the complementary function. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡6x),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x} & =(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡6x)+6x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡6x) \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =12(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)-36x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡6x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n12(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)-36x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡6x)+36x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡6x)=-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n-12\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+12\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡6x=-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}12\\beta =-12\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x) \\\\ -12\\alpha =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =0$ and $\\beta =-1.$ Therefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/state.json" "file_sha256" "db29583229ee19e7ec41ee5464bc69bf5bded44515119337e03a03b2fd10bc34"} {"question" "q-93824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "04f0f5b03a1eed193771446f42328616d0f5d26cce05874a2cf5e6f422fce0ed"} {"question" "q-93824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/state.json" "file_sha256" "db29583229ee19e7ec41ee5464bc69bf5bded44515119337e03a03b2fd10bc34"} {"question" "q-93824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}_{p}=-3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x"] ["math" "{y}_{p}=-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x"] ["math" "{y}_{p}=2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+5x\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x"] ["math" "{y}_{p}=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x"] ["math" "{y}_{p}=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/state.json" "file_sha256" "db29583229ee19e7ec41ee5464bc69bf5bded44515119337e03a03b2fd10bc34"} {"question" "q-93824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}_{p}=-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/state.json" "file_sha256" "db29583229ee19e7ec41ee5464bc69bf5bded44515119337e03a03b2fd10bc34"} {"question" "q-93834" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-3\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y=20\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny(x)=A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{2x}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x,\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-3\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y=20\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x,\\,y(0)=3,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/state.json" "file_sha256" "db29583229ee19e7ec41ee5464bc69bf5bded44515119337e03a03b2fd10bc34"} {"question" "q-93834" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ by substituting the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=3$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & =A{e}^{0}+B{e}^{2(0)}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2(0)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2(0) \\\\ 3 & =A+B-1 \\\\ 4 & =A+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Differentiating $y$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=A{e}^{x}+2B{e}^{2x}-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=0$ into the derivative gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =A{e}^{0}+2B{e}^{2(0)}-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2(0)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2(0) \\\\ 0 & =A+2B-6 \\\\ 6 & =A+2B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following system of equations for $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}A+B=4 \\\\ A+2B=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=2,B=2.$\n\nFinally, since $A=2$ and $B=2,$ we have the following solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\ny=2{e}^{x}+2{e}^{2x}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/state.json" "file_sha256" "db29583229ee19e7ec41ee5464bc69bf5bded44515119337e03a03b2fd10bc34"} {"question" "q-93834" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "04f0f5b03a1eed193771446f42328616d0f5d26cce05874a2cf5e6f422fce0ed"} {"question" "q-93834" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072308/state.json" "file_sha256" "db29583229ee19e7ec41ee5464bc69bf5bded44515119337e03a03b2fd10bc34"} {"question" "q-93834" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-3{e}^{x}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x"] ["math" "y=2{e}^{x}+2{e}^{2x}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x"] ["math" "y=5{e}^{x}-{e}^{2x}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x"] ["math" "y=6{e}^{2x}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\